cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the associated article."
title: "Code for: Slow cooling and the geomagnetic polarity history link protracted thermoviscous remagnetization to superchrons"
abstract: "Code and derived data for Pescarini et al., submitted to Geophysical Journal International. The scripts model thermoviscous resetting and continuous-cooling blocking of single-domain pyrrhotite and magnetite, and the vector cancellation of the acquired moment under a stochastic geomagnetic polarity history. The remagnetized carbonates of the Nama Group (Namibia) are the case study; the TROUT unmixing of the demagnetization data and the Raman thermometry that constrain the model are included. It also includes the specimen selection applied to the TROUT spectra. The scripts reproduce Figs 1 and 3–7 and Tables S1–S7."
authors:
